---
const traceSteps = [
  { id: 'source', label: 'Read source', script: 'Read hello.py as the main module.', imported: 'Find hello.py while resolving import hello.' },
  { id: 'compile', label: 'Compile', script: 'Parse source → AST → code object → bytecode in memory.', imported: 'Validate the cached .pyc. Compile only when it is missing or invalid.' },
  { id: 'execute', label: 'Execute', script: 'Run the code object as __main__ in CPython’s evaluation loop.', imported: 'Run the module code once, then store the module in sys.modules.' },
  { id: 'result', label: 'Observe', script: 'Print hi. A normal main-script run does not write hello.py to __pycache__.', imported: 'Print loaded. A valid hello.cpython-*.pyc now exists for a later import.' },
];
---

<section class="learning-lab" data-learning-lab aria-labelledby="lab-title">
  <header class="lab-header">
    <p class="lab-kicker">Python Learning Lab 01 · predict → trace → break → explain</p>
    <h2 id="lab-title">Does Python always reuse <code>.pyc</code> bytecode?</h2>
    <p>Choose before revealing the execution path. The distinction is not “compiled versus interpreted”—both paths compile to a code object.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="lab-section lab-predict" data-stage="predict">
    <div class="section-number">01</div>
    <div>
      <h3>Predict</h3>
      <p>After running <code>python hello.py</code>, what normally happens to <code>__pycache__</code>?</p>
      <div class="choice-grid" role="group" aria-label="Prediction choices">
        <button type="button" data-predict="writes">A. CPython writes <code>hello.pyc</code></button>
        <button type="button" data-predict="memory">B. CPython compiles in memory; no import cache is written</button>
        <button type="button" data-predict="none">C. Source executes directly without compilation</button>
      </div>
      <p class="feedback" data-predict-feedback aria-live="polite">Commit to an answer before tracing the runtime.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="lab-section">
    <div class="section-number">02</div>
    <div class="trace-content">
      <h3>Trace two different entry points</h3>
      <div class="mode-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Execution mode">
        <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-mode="script"><code>python hello.py</code></button>
        <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-mode="import"><code>import hello</code></button>
      </div>

      <div class="trace-layout">
        <ol class="trace-path" aria-label="CPython execution trace">
          {traceSteps.map((step, index) => (
            <li>
              <button type="button" data-trace-step={index} aria-current={index === 0 ? 'step' : undefined}>
                <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
                {step.label}
              </button>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
        <div class="trace-panel" aria-live="polite">
          <p class="trace-label" data-trace-label>Step 1 · Read source</p>
          <p data-trace-copy>{traceSteps[0].script}</p>
          <pre data-trace-code><code>$ python hello.py
hi
$ test -d __pycache__ || echo "no cache"
no cache</code></pre>
          <div class="trace-nav">
            <button type="button" data-prev>← Previous</button>
            <span data-progress>1 / 4</span>
            <button type="button" data-next>Next →</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="lab-section">
    <div class="section-number">03</div>
    <div>
      <h3>Break the imported-module cache</h3>
      <p>Imports may reuse <code>__pycache__/hello.cpython-*.pyc</code>. Change the source and CPython invalidates the timestamp-based cache.</p>
      <label class="break-toggle">
        <input type="checkbox" data-stale />
        Change <code>hello.py</code> after its first import
      </label>
      <div class="cache-route" data-cache-route aria-live="polite">
        <span>import hello</span><b>→</b><span>valid .pyc</span><b>→</b><span>reuse bytecode</span><b>→</b><span>execute</span>
      </div>
      <p class="lab-note">For timestamp-based caches, CPython compares stored source metadata. Hash-based <code>.pyc</code> files follow the validation mode described by PEP 552.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="lab-section">
    <div class="section-number">04</div>
    <div>
      <h3>Explain it back</h3>
      <p>Why can <code>import hello</code> reuse cached bytecode while <code>python hello.py</code> normally does not?</p>
      <button type="button" class="reveal" data-reveal aria-expanded="false">Reveal a model explanation</button>
      <div class="model-answer" data-answer hidden>
        <p>Both paths compile source into a code object before execution. The import system additionally manages a reusable on-disk cache because modules may be imported again. A directly executed source file becomes <code>__main__</code>; CPython compiles it for that run but normally does not create an import-cache entry for it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="lab-section java-bridge">
    <div class="section-number">05</div>
    <div>
      <h3>Transfer from Java</h3>
      <div class="compare-grid">
        <div><strong>Java</strong><span><code>javac</code> creates a persistent <code>.class</code> artifact before the JVM runs it.</span></div>
        <div><strong>Python</strong><span>CPython creates code objects at runtime; reusable <code>.pyc</code> files belong mainly to the import cache.</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="checkpoint"><strong>Checkpoint:</strong> Python is compiled <em>and</em> interpreted. Those words describe different stages, not competing language categories.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  const roots = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-learning-lab]');
  const steps = [
    { label: 'Read source', script: 'Read hello.py as the main module.', imported: 'Find hello.py while resolving import hello.' },
    { label: 'Compile', script: 'Parse source → AST → code object → bytecode in memory.', imported: 'Validate the cached .pyc. Compile only when it is missing or invalid.' },
    { label: 'Execute', script: 'Run the code object as __main__ in CPython’s evaluation loop.', imported: 'Run the module code once, then store the module in sys.modules.' },
    { label: 'Observe', script: 'Print hi. A normal main-script run does not write hello.py to __pycache__.', imported: 'Print loaded. A valid hello.cpython-*.pyc now exists for a later import.' },
  ];
  const code = {
    script: `$ python hello.py\nhi\n$ test -d __pycache__ || echo "no cache"\nno cache`,
    import: `$ python -c "import hello"\nloaded\n$ ls __pycache__\nhello.cpython-*.pyc`,
  };

  roots.forEach((root) => {
    let mode: 'script' | 'import' = 'script';
    let active = 0;
    const stepButtons = Array.from(root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-trace-step]'));
    const label = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-trace-label]');
    const copy = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-trace-copy]');
    const codeBlock = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-trace-code] code');
    const progress = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-progress]');

    const renderTrace = () => {
      stepButtons.forEach((button, index) => {
        if (index === active) button.setAttribute('aria-current', 'step');
        else button.removeAttribute('aria-current');
      });
      const step = steps[active];
      if (label) label.textContent = `Step ${active + 1} · ${step.label}`;
      if (copy) copy.textContent = mode === 'script' ? step.script : step.imported;
      if (codeBlock) codeBlock.textContent = code[mode];
      if (progress) progress.textContent = `${active + 1} / ${steps.length}`;
    };

    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-mode]').forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener('click', () => {
        mode = button.dataset.mode === 'import' ? 'import' : 'script';
        root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-mode]').forEach((tab) =>
          tab.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(tab === button)),
        );
        active = 0;
        renderTrace();
      });
    });
    stepButtons.forEach((button, index) => button.addEventListener('click', () => { active = index; renderTrace(); }));
    root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-prev]')?.addEventListener('click', () => { active = Math.max(0, active - 1); renderTrace(); });
    root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-next]')?.addEventListener('click', () => { active = Math.min(steps.length - 1, active + 1); renderTrace(); });

    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-predict]').forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const correct = button.dataset.predict === 'memory';
        root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-predict]').forEach((choice) => {
          choice.classList.toggle('is-correct', choice.dataset.predict === 'memory');
          choice.classList.toggle('is-wrong', choice === button && !correct);
          choice.disabled = true;
        });
        const feedback = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-predict-feedback]');
        if (feedback) feedback.textContent = correct
          ? 'Correct. The main script is compiled for this process, but not normally written to the import cache.'
          : 'Not quite. CPython still compiles the source—but a normal main-script run does not write the import cache.';
      });
    });

    root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-stale]')?.addEventListener('change', (event) => {
      const stale = (event.currentTarget as HTMLInputElement).checked;
      const route = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-cache-route]');
      if (route) route.innerHTML = stale
        ? '<span>import hello</span><b>→</b><span>invalid .pyc</span><b>→</b><span>recompile source</span><b>→</b><span>execute</span>'
        : '<span>import hello</span><b>→</b><span>valid .pyc</span><b>→</b><span>reuse bytecode</span><b>→</b><span>execute</span>';
    });

    root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-reveal]')?.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
      const button = event.currentTarget as HTMLButtonElement;
      const answer = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-answer]');
      const expanded = button.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
      button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!expanded));
      button.textContent = expanded ? 'Reveal a model explanation' : 'Hide model explanation';
      if (answer) answer.hidden = expanded;
    });
    renderTrace();
  });
</script>

<style>
  .learning-lab { border: 1px solid var(--color-border); background: var(--color-surface); }
  .lab-header, .lab-section { padding: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 1.5rem); }
  .lab-header { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); background: var(--color-bg); }
  .lab-header h2 { margin: 0.35rem 0 0.65rem; color: var(--color-text); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 3vw, 1.55rem); }
  .lab-header p, .lab-section p { color: var(--color-text-dim); line-height: 1.65; }
  .lab-kicker, .trace-label { margin: 0; color: var(--color-accent) !important; font: 700 0.72rem/1.4 var(--font-mono); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
  .lab-section { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2.2rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .lab-section:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .section-number { color: var(--color-text-muted); font: 700 0.75rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); }
  .lab-section h3 { margin: 0 0 0.65rem; color: var(--color-text); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 1rem; }
  .choice-grid { display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; }
  button { font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .choice-grid button, .mode-tabs button, .trace-nav button, .reveal {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border); background: var(--color-bg); color: var(--color-text-dim);
    padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; cursor: pointer; text-align: left;
  }
  button:hover:not(:disabled), button:focus-visible { border-color: var(--color-accent); color: var(--color-text); outline: none; }
  .choice-grid button.is-correct { border-color: var(--color-green); color: var(--color-green); }
  .choice-grid button.is-wrong { border-color: var(--color-rose); color: var(--color-rose); }
  .choice-grid button:disabled { cursor: default; opacity: 0.82; }
  .feedback { min-height: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 0; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.78rem; }
  .mode-tabs { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .mode-tabs button[aria-selected='true'] { border-color: var(--color-accent); color: var(--color-text); box-shadow: inset 0 -2px var(--color-accent); }
  .trace-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(9rem, 0.65fr) minmax(0, 1.35fr); gap: 0.75rem; }
  .trace-path { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .trace-path li:not(:last-child)::after { content: '↓'; display: block; padding: 0.15rem 0 0.15rem 1rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  .trace-path button { width: 100%; display: flex; gap: 0.65rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); background: var(--color-bg); color: var(--color-text-dim); padding: 0.6rem; cursor: pointer; text-align: left; }
  .trace-path button span { color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  .trace-path button[aria-current='step'] { border-color: var(--color-accent); color: var(--color-text); }
  .trace-panel { border: 1px solid var(--color-border); background: var(--color-bg); padding: 0.85rem; }
  .trace-panel pre { margin: 0.75rem 0; padding: 0.75rem; overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); background: var(--color-surface); color: var(--color-text); font: 0.75rem/1.6 var(--font-mono); }
  .trace-nav { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.55rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); font: 0.75rem/1.4 var(--font-mono); }
  .trace-nav button { padding: 0.4rem 0.55rem; }
  .break-toggle { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.55rem; color: var(--color-text); font: 0.8rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); }
  .cache-route { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 0.45rem; margin-top: 0.8rem; font: 0.75rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); }
  .cache-route span { border: 1px solid var(--color-border); background: var(--color-bg); color: var(--color-text); padding: 0.4rem 0.55rem; }
  .cache-route b { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .lab-note { font-size: 0.78rem; }
  .reveal { margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .model-answer { padding: 0.1rem 0.8rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent); background: var(--color-bg); }
  .model-answer[hidden] { display: none; }
  .compare-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .compare-grid div { border: 1px solid var(--color-border); background: var(--color-bg); padding: 0.8rem; }
  .compare-grid strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; color: var(--color-accent); font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .compare-grid span { color: var(--color-text-dim); font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .checkpoint { margin-bottom: 0; }
  code { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--color-text); }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .lab-section { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.35rem; }
    .trace-layout, .compare-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .mode-tabs { flex-direction: column; }
  }
</style>
